    description: "Screenshots should be saved to .agent/tracker-workspace/screenshots/ (not .agent/screenshots/) so they inherit the same group ownership (project-dev, 2775) as ops files. The /tmp fallback should be removed once this works.\n\nTaking a screenshot should create a brand new tracker item (not associate with the currently selected item — that item might be about hypergumbo the analyzer, not the tracker). Flow:\n1. User presses S, draws annotations, confirms\n2. SVG saved to .agent/tracker-workspace/screenshots/screenshot-<timestamp>.svg\n3. A new work_item is auto-created via TrackerSet with title \"Screenshot <timestamp>\", status needs_human_review, and the SVG path embedded in the description or first discussion entry\n4. The TUI shows a notification: \"Screenshot saved, tracker item WI-xxxxx created\"\n5. The user can then navigate to that item and add context via discussion\n\nThis creates a ticket-like workflow where screenshots are first-class tracker items. The inline preview (ADR-0020 Part 2) will render them when cairosvg+chafa are available. Labels from WI-gikut (numbered markers + text) become the annotation content within the item.\n\nKey files:\n- packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/annotations.py (screenshot_path)\n- packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/tui.py (action_capture_screenshot, _on_annotation_result)"  # 3693
